VI. finished stuffs

4. Align repo content ingestion format to mirror render output format
    [x] 'content/backend/asset_ingestion/ingestion_parser.py': Create standalone parser helper
        - Accepts a raw string, returns a result with: creates list[(path, content)], updates list[(path, content)], deletes list[path], errors list[str]
        - Scans line by line; on hitting `¤ (create|update): (.+?) ¤` begins a content block, collects lines until the identical closing bookend; strips triple backticks from the content
        - On hitting `¤ delete: (.+?) ¤` records a standalone delete entry, no content
        - Error case: opening bookend for create/update with no matching closing bookend before EOF → append to errors
        - No dependency on DiskPort, entities, or ErrorCollector — pure string → structured lists
    [x] 'content/backend/asset_ingestion/ingestion_service.py': Refactor `apply_file_changes` to delegate to the parser
        - Call the parser with `raw_text`
        - Iterate creates → `self.files.write_file(path, content)`
        - Iterate updates → `self.files.write_file(path, content)`
        - Iterate deletes → `self.files.delete_file(path)`
        - Collect per-operation exceptions into the errors list
        - Return `d.IngestApplyResult(written, deleted, errors)` as before
        - Remove the old regex machinery (`file_header_pattern`, `cleaned_file_pattern`, `delete_pattern`, `_clean_content`)


